Now spawn point and camYaw. Let me set spawn at (-30,0,0) with camYaw = Math.PI/2 (camera to +x, looking -x down a road? Actually at x=-30 there's a road at x=-30). Looking -x means looking toward x=-280. Buildings on both sides. Hmm.

Actually let me spawn on the beach side looking at the city skyline: player at (30,0,0), camYaw=Math.PI/2 (camera at +x ~37, looking -x toward city). That shows city to the west, beach in foreground. Good for RP.

But mission 1 target is (-70,-40) which is in the city. Fine.

Let me update reset spawn and initial camera.

Also update the initial camera position line.

Current reset:
```js
this.player.position.set(-70,0,20);
this.camYaw=0;this.camPitch=0.18;
S.camYaw=0;S.camPitch=0.18;
...
this.camera.position.set(-70,5,30);
```

Let me change to:
```js
this.player.position.set(30,0,0);
this.camYaw=Math.PI/2;this.camPitch=0.16;
S.camYaw=Math.PI/2;S.camPitch=0.16;
...
this.camera.position.set(38,4,0);
```

Wait, if camYaw=PI/2, camera at player + (sin(PI/2)*cosPitch*7, ..., cos(PI/2)*...) = (30+~7, y, 0) = (37, y, 0). Looking toward player (30,1.3,0) i.e., facing -x. Good.

Let me also set the initial camera position accordingly and lookAt.

Let me edit.

