Now dispose: set renderer=null to avoid old resize errors, and clear scene references. Let me improve:
```js
Game.prototype.dispose=function(){
  if(this.renderer){this.renderer.dispose();this.renderer=null;}
  this.ready=false;this.locked=false;
  if(document.pointerLockElement)document.exitPointerLock();
};
```
But if renderer=null, the old resize handler `if(!this.renderer)return;` guards. Good. Also app.loop only calls current game. Good.

But careful: after dispose, `this.scene` still exists with geometries; not freed but fine. Setting renderer=null means if something calls this.renderer.render it errors. app.loop checks `this.game` which is the new game after quit+enter. Between quit (game=null) and enter, app.loop sees no game. Good.

Let me edit dispose.

Also, I should ensure that when re-entering after quit, the old window resize listener still calls old game.resize() which now returns early (renderer null). Good.

Let me edit.

